# NickelTiles (libnickeltiles.so)
#
# Turns the Kobo home screen into a grid of app tiles. Built on NickelHook,
# like NickelMenu and NickelHome. Firmware 4.23.15505+ home screen layout;
# developed and tested on 4.45.23697.
#
# What the grid shows
#   - "Continue reading": the most recently opened book across KOReader
#     (history.lua), Plato (.metadata.json) and Kobo's reader (KoboReader.sqlite),
#     with title, author, progress and the book's cover (EPUB, KEPUB, FB2,
#     FB2.ZIP, MOBI, AZW, AZW3, PRC, CBZ; cached under covers/). Other formats,
#     such as PDF, show a book icon. Tapping opens it in the app that last read it.
#     nt_recent_source: auto (default) | koreader | plato | nickel.
#     nt_recent_info: which of title, author, progress the caption shows.
#     nt_recent_cover: 1 shows the book's cover (default), 0 a book icon.
#   - Sleep screen: with "Show book covers full screen" on (Settings >
#     Energy saving and privacy), the sleep cover is that same book, from
#     whichever app read it last. Kept as .kobo/screensaver/nt-recent.<ext>,
#     refreshed as the reader goes to sleep. nt_sleep_cover:0 turns it off.
#   - One tile per NickelMenu main-menu entry (KOBOeReader/.adds/nm/*). Add,
#     remove or rename entries there and the grid follows at the next boot.
#     Supported actions: cmd_spawn, cmd_output, power, nickel_misc
#     (force_usb_connection, home, rescan_books), nickel_wifi, dbg_toast and
#     chain_success/chain_failure/chain_always. Others show a toast.
#   - Extra tiles from tile: lines in the config.
#
# Using it
#   - The "Tiles settings" tile (gear) opens a settings page with tabs along
#     the bottom: Layout (tiles per row, tile size, Kobo's home rows), Books
#     (the Continue reading tile, how many recent books get a tile and where
#     they come from, the sleep screen cover), Tiles (which tiles are shown)
#     and Help (short explanations, the NickelMenu switch, add-on repair).
#     Save applies at once; Cancel leaves everything as it was.
#     Switched-off add-ons: NickelHook add-ons a crash left off (NickelMenu,
#     KPM, NickelHome, ...); Repair turns them back on, then restart.
#   - Tap a tile: it darkens while pressed and runs when released.
#   - More tiles than fit: swipe left or right, or use the arrows under the
#     tiles, to change page.
#   - Long-press a tile (about 0.7 s): it gets a thick frame (arrange mode).
#     Tap another tile to swap the two; tap the same tile to cancel. The new
#     order is saved to the config (order: line).
#
# Configuration: KOBOeReader/.adds/nickel-tiles/config (key:value, # comments,
# reboot to apply). See the default file for every key.
#   nt_enabled, nt_log, nt_actions, nt_kobo_rows, nt_recent, nt_recent_count, nt_recent_source, nt_recent_info, nt_recent_cover,
#   nt_sleep_cover, nt_columns, nt_tile_px, hide:<label>, icon:<label>:<png>, order:<a>|<b>|..,
#   tile:<label>:<icon>:<command>
#
# Icons: icons/<slug>.png in this folder, where <slug> is the label in lower
# case with runs of other characters replaced by '-' (e.g. "kpm - Status" ->
# kpm-status.png). Square PNGs, 200x200 recommended. Missing icon: a letter
# tile is drawn.
#
# Uninstall: create an empty file named "uninstall" in this folder and reboot,
# or delete this folder. The mod removes itself on the next start.
#
# Failsafe: if Nickel dies within 3 seconds of the mod loading, the mod stays
# disabled on the next boot (NickelHook renames it out of the way). Reinstall
# the package to re-enable it. Do not launch an app in the first seconds after
# the home screen appears.
#
# If something goes wrong: NickelMenu > "NickelTiles off/on" (offered on first
# start, or Tiles settings > Help > Off/on switch in NickelMenu) turns the tiles off
# and restarts. If Kobo crashes three times in a row within 30 seconds of
# starting, NickelTiles turns itself off and offers to turn back on. Over USB:
# nt_enabled:0 in config. Crashes are always written to nickel-tiles.log.
#
